cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Gridalyn: a governed SDK for distribution-network digital twins and flexibility studies"
message: "If you use this software or its studies in your research, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Henao
    given-names: Nilson
    affiliation: "LIREI, Université du Québec à Trois-Rivières"
    email: nilson.henao@uqtr.ca
repository-code: "https://github.com/lirei-lab/gridalyn"
url: "https://lirei-lab.github.io/gridalyn"
abstract: >-
  Gridalyn models, simulates and optimizes multi-scale electric distribution
  systems and their distributed energy resources: flexible building loads, EV
  chargers and storage. Declarative YAML StudyProject and Workflow contracts
  drive synthetic data generation, a digital twin, pandapower/lightsim power
  flow and flexibility-market operations, emitting governed report artifacts
  with regression baselines so that a published result can be re-derived from
  its configuration.
keywords:
  - distribution networks
  - digital twin
  - electric vehicles
  - hosting capacity
  - demand flexibility
  - power systems
  - reproducible research
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
